# DO NOT DEPLOY THIS FILE.
#
# This is an example template only. The production Secret is managed outside Git
# via the Helm chart's `existingSecret` mechanism (see deploy/helm/commoncal-mcp/values.yaml
# and deploy/flux/overlays/production/charts/mcp-helmrelease.yaml).
#
# For reference, the Secret must contain at minimum:
#   mcp-internal-api-key  — shared key between MCP server and backend (x-mcp-api-key header)
#   mcp-session-secret    — session encryption key used by the MCP server
#
# Creation example (if not using an external secret provider):
#   kubectl create secret generic commoncal-mcp-secrets \
#     --namespace commoncal \
#     --from-literal=mcp-internal-api-key='<random-32-byte-hex>' \
#     --from-literal=mcp-session-secret='<random-32-byte-hex>' \
#     --dry-run=client | kubectl apply -f -
#
# Rotation procedure:
#   1. Generate a new mcp-internal-api-key and mcp-session-secret.
#   2. Update the Secret in the cluster (kubectl set or external-secret controller).
#   3. Both old and new keys must be accepted during a grace period — update the
#      backend and MCP server to accept the previous key for 24 hours.
#   4. After the grace period, remove the old key from validation.
